{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap","requirement":"A landlord may not demand or receive security above one month's rent in addition to the first month's rent paid at occupancy; qualifying small landlords may take up to two months' rent.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 2 months' rent for qualifying small landlords","coverage_conditions":"Security for a residential rental agreement used as the tenant's dwelling. A natural person, or an LLC whose members are all natural persons, owning no more than two rental properties with no more than four dwelling units total may take up to two months' rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Residential property used as the tenant's dwelling"},"exemptions":"Advance payment of six months' rent or more where the lease term is six months or longer; voluntary mutual agreement for alterations; higher security charged to a service member is excluded from the two-month small-landlord limit; subdivision does not apply to security collected or demanded before July 1, 2024.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(c) (1) Except as provided in paragraph (2), (3), or (5), a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to one month’s rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Deposit return within 21 days with itemized statement","requirement":"No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant vacates, the landlord must give the tenant an itemized statement of the security received and its disposition and return any remaining security.","key_value":"21 calendar days","coverage_conditions":"Security for a residential rental agreement used as the tenant's dwelling.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential property used as the tenant's dwelling"},"exemptions":"The document-production requirements do not apply where deductions for repairs and cleaning together do not exceed $125, or where the tenant signs a waiver at or after a termination notice; a tenant may still request documentation within 14 calendar days.","penalty":"A landlord who in bad faith fails to comply with the return and itemization subdivision is not entitled to claim any amount of the security.","effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(h) (1) No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant has vacated the premises, but not earlier than the time that either the landlord or the tenant provides a notice to terminate the tenancy under Section 1946 or 1946.1, Section 1161 of the Code of Civil Procedure, or not earlier than 60 calendar days prior to the expiration of a fixed-term lease, the landlord shall furnish the tenant, a copy of an itemized statement indicating the basis for, and the amount of, any security received and the disposition of the security, and shall return any remaining portion of the security to the tenant as follows:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Service member higher security disclosure and return","requirement":"A landlord charging a service member higher than standard security must give a written statement before the lease is signed of the amount and the reason, and must return the additional security after no more than six months of residency if rent is not in arrears.","key_value":"extra security returned after no more than 6 months of residency","coverage_conditions":"A service member who rents residential property in which the service member will reside and is charged higher than standard or advertised security because of credit history, credit score, housing history or another tenant-related factor.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Security charged to a service member as defined in Section 400 of the Military and Veterans Code"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-04-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"On or after April 1, 2025, if a landlord or its agent charges a service member who rents residential property in which the service member will reside a higher than standard or advertised security pursuant to paragraph (1) due to the credit history, credit score, housing history, or other factor related to the tenant, the landlord shall provide the tenant with a written statement, on or before the date the lease is signed, of the amount of the higher security and an explanation why the higher security amount is being charged. The additional amount of security shall be returned to the tenant after no more than six months of residency if the tenant is not in arrears for any rent due during that period.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
